{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNW"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.sytDim_pos_of_mem_partsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.sytDim_pos_of_mem_partsOf","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.lean#L85-L89","doc":"The hypothesis in exactly the form the pincer bridge theorems consume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.sytDim_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.sytDim_pos","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.lean#L73-L83","doc":"**Dimension positivity** (the pincer's hypothesis, proved): `0 < sytDim l` for sorted\npositive lists — `numSYTenum · prodHooks = n! > 0` forces `numSYTenum > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.sytDim_eq_numSYTenum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.sytDim_eq_numSYTenum","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.lean#L59-L71","doc":"**`sytDim` is the genuine `#SYT` count**: the kernel's hook-length dimension equals the\nenumeration count `numSYTenum` (sorted positive lists), via the hook-product bridge and the\nmachine-checked FRT identity `numSYTenum · prodHooks = n!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.hookProd_eq_prodHooks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.hookProd_eq_prodHooks","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.lean#L43-L57","doc":"**The two list-level hook products agree** on sorted lists: the kernel's\n`λ_i + λ'_j − j − i − 1` and `IdentityI`'s `(λ_i − j) + (colLen_j − i) − 1` compute the same hook\nat every genuine cell, because `j < λ_i` (cell bound) and `i < λ'_j` (staircase) make both\nℕ-subtractions non-truncating. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.colLen_eq_countP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.colLen_eq_countP","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.lean#L37-L41","doc":"`IdentityI.colLen` is `countP` (filter-length form). ","signatureChunk":0}]}